<title>USA: DOW CHANGES DIRECTION, FALLS 50 POINTS.</title>
<headline>DOW CHANGES DIRECTION, FALLS 50 POINTS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dow Jones industrial average changed direction in mid-morning trading Wednesday and lost more than 50 points as bonds retreated from their early highs.</p>
<p>At 10:22 a.m. EDT(/1422 GMT), the Dow was down 52.26 points at 7,908.58 after soaring nearly 80 points initially.</p>
